    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_8bb95856",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image features a close-up of actor Morgan Freeman with a skeptical, slightly amused expression. The text overlaid on the image reads: 'i don't understand your specific kind of stupid. but i do admire your total commitment to it.' The overall intent of this meme is to convey a sarcastic, dismissive, and mildly mocking tone toward someone whose behavior or belief is perceived as foolish or irrational, but whose dedication to it is noteworthy. The meme uses Morgan Freeman’s iconic, calm, and wise persona to deliver a biting commentary. The intent is not to target any specific group or individual based on protected characteristics, nor does it contain abusive, cyberbullying, harmful, hateful, misogynous, or propagandistic content. The humor stems from the juxtaposition of Freeman’s dignified demeanor with the crude, self-deprecatingly sarcastic text, which is often used to mock someone’s stubbornness or irrationality in a lighthearted, non-harmful way. The meme is a form of internet humor that relies on irony and the contrast between the image and text, not on targeting or degrading any group or individual.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_5b12556e"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
